# Valgrind memcheck suppressions for ct-ctgrind.
# Add suppressions here if CI surfaces false positives from test
# infrastructure (inventory registration, Rust runtime init, etc.)
# that are unrelated to the krabipqc CT paths under test.

# Suppress Memcheck:Value8 for the positive decaps fixtures. SHAKE-256 absorbs
# tainted z into Keccak u64 state; Keccak ops (XOR, theta/chi/rho/pi) are
# branch-free, so Value8 is a false positive. Memcheck:Cond is NOT suppressed,
# so real CT violations still trip the gate.
{
   mlkem-decaps-shake-z-x86
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:ct_fix__mlkem_decaps__*
}
# Same false positive on aarch64 where the compiler outlines the Keccak
# round function into a separate symbol.  The wildcard on the function
# name makes the suppression stable across code changes that shift the
# OUTLINED_FUNCTION_N index; the caller frame narrows it to the decaps
# fixtures so real leaks in other outlined code still trip.
{
   mlkem-decaps-shake-z-aarch64-outlined
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:OUTLINED_FUNCTION_*
   fun:ct_fix__mlkem_decaps__*
}
